::ENG2_U02_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.R.02] Passage A: Jonas almost pulled Mina's uneven tomato seeds from the tray, but he remembered his own first garden and chose to label the row with her. Passage B: Talia gave Andre her spare blazer even though she had saved for it, and Andre competed confidently. Question: Which is the best shared theme statement for both passages?{
=A. Helping others may require giving up something we value.#Correct. Both Jonas and Talia sacrifice something they wanted to protect in order to support someone else.
~B. Gardening is easier than debate.#Incorrect. This compares topics on the surface but does not state a universal theme.
~C. Prepared people never need help.#Incorrect. Andre needs help even though Talia prepared carefully.
~D. Teams always win competitions.#Incorrect. This is too absolute and does not apply to both passages.
}

::ENG2_U02_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.R.02] Passage A: Jonas wanted the garden to look perfect, but he decided not to pull Mina's uneven row. Weeks later, the crooked row grew taller than any other. Passage B: Talia handed Andre the spare blazer before he walked onstage. Question: How does Passage A develop the theme?{
~A. Jonas wins a garden contest.#Incorrect. The passage never says Jonas wins a contest.
~B. Mina teaches Jonas how to plant.#Incorrect. Mina's planting matters, but the theme develops through Jonas's choice to support her.
=C. Jonas chooses to support Mina instead of fixing the imperfect row.#Correct. Jonas gives up control and learns that helping matters more than perfection.
~D. The visitors cancel their trip.#Incorrect. There is no evidence that visitors cancel.
}

::ENG2_U02_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.R.02] Passage A: Jonas lets Mina's uneven row stay. Passage B: Talia thinks about how long she saved for the spare blazer, then gives it to Andre so he can compete. Question: How does Passage B develop the theme?{
~A. Talia refuses to help Andre.#Incorrect. Talia helps Andre by giving him the blazer.
=B. Talia gives Andre the spare blazer even though she saved for it.#Correct. Her sacrifice develops the theme that helping may require giving up something valuable.
~C. Andre decides not to compete.#Incorrect. Andre walks onstage after Talia helps him.
~D. The team loses because of the rain.#Incorrect. The passage says the team wins.
}

::ENG2_U02_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.R.02] Passage A: Jonas gives up his need for a perfect garden row. Passage B: Talia gives up wearing her spare blazer so Andre can compete. Question: Which comparison is most accurate?{
~A. Both passages show characters avoiding responsibility.#Incorrect. Jonas and Talia both act responsibly by helping someone else.
~B. Passage A is about competition, and Passage B is about gardening.#Incorrect. This reverses the passages and does not compare theme development.
~C. Both passages show that sacrifice is always punished.#Incorrect. The outcomes are positive in both passages.
=D. Both passages show characters choosing to help someone else, but Jonas gives up control while Talia gives up a personal item.#Correct. This compares how each text develops the same theme differently.
}

::ENG2_U02_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.R.02] Passage A: Jonas says, "Let's label this row together, and we can watch what happens." Passage B: Andre arrives with rain soaking his jacket and panic tightening his voice, so Talia hands him the spare blazer. Question: Which evidence from Passage B best supports the theme?{
~A. Talia kept an extra uniform in her locker.#Incorrect. This shows preparation, but not the moment of sacrifice.
=B. Talia handed Andre the blazer when he arrived soaked and nervous.#Correct. This directly shows Talia helping Andre by giving up something useful to her.
~C. Andre walked onstage.#Incorrect. This shows what happened after the help, but not Talia's sacrifice.
~D. Talia wore an old sweater.#Incorrect. This supports sacrifice indirectly, but the clearest evidence is her choice to hand Andre the blazer.
}
